The Inclusion Toolkit has two licences: one for its content, and one for its code.


CONTENT: CREATIVE COMMONS ATTRIBUTION 4.0 INTERNATIONAL (CC BY 4.0)

The toolkit's content is shared under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The content is:

- the text of each resource, in src/content/toolkit
- the glossary and abbreviations, in src/content/glossary.ts and src/content/abbreviations.ts
- the Word, PowerPoint and PDF files, in public/files and toolkit-sources/branded

You can share and change the content, for any purpose, as long as you give credit, link to the
licence, and say if you made changes. Please credit it like this:

  Abi Harrison-Nye first made the Inclusion Toolkit for giffgaff and HAND (Home of Accessibility
  and NeuroDiversity), with Bim Williams and Pranay Gandhi, and it has been updated and added to
  since. Shared under CC BY 4.0.

The fonts inside the Word, PowerPoint and PDF files, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next and Atkinson
Hyperlegible Mono, have their own licence, the SIL Open Font License, version 1.1.


